          "en": "Public Proclamation, Migration, and the Supreme Victory: Commanded: 'O you cloaked! Arise and warn!' (74:1-2), the Prophet ﷺ initiated the call to monotheism privately for three years, with early converts including Abu Bakr, Ali, Khadijah, and Zayd. Commanded to declare the message openly (15:94), he summoned Quraysh from Mount Safa, meeting bitter hostility. Early converts (Bilal, Ammar, Khabbab) endured immense torture with unyielding patience until the Hijrah to Madinah, where the Ansar embraced them with boundless brotherhood. The Islamic state arose, persevering through Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah. In the 8th year of Hijrah, Makkah surrendered in supreme triumph. Entering humbly, the Prophet ﷺ dismantled all 360 idols surrounding the Ka'bah reciting 17:81, granting universal amnesty: 'Go, for you are free!'",
